@startuml layers
' Paint order, top to bottom. Blitz hoists an element out of its parent's
' paint order only when it is positioned AND has a non-zero z-index
' (blitz-paint paint_tree.rs). Everything else paints in document order,
' and the page sub-documents paint with #main.
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 6
  BorderColor #52687A
  FontColor #182734
}
title Layers: what paints over what (top is nearest the viewer)

rectangle "<b>z-index 40</b>   hover labels  <i>.tip</i>\nshown by :hover > .tip { visibility: visible }\npointer-events: none" as tips #F4CCCC
rectangle "<b>z-index 30</b>   address suggestions  <i>#suggestions</i>\nabsolute under #urlwrap; empty → display:none" as sugg #FCE4D6
rectangle "<b>z-index 6</b>   floating find box  <i>#findbar</i>\nabsolute, top-right of #main; hidden with visibility" as find #FFF2CC
rectangle "<b>z-index 2</b>   find highlights  <i>#findoverlay .findhit</i>\nabsolute, inset 0 over #main; pointer-events: none" as overlay #FFF9E5
rectangle "<b>z-index auto</b>   chrome boxes in document order\nrows, row actions (absolute, z auto), cards, menus, status" as chrome #E2EFDA
rectangle "<b>page sub-documents</b>   one RhoDocument per tab\npainted as part of #main, below every hoisted layer" as pages #DDEBF7

tips -[hidden]down-> sugg
sugg -[hidden]down-> find
find -[hidden]down-> overlay
overlay -[hidden]down-> chrome
chrome -[hidden]down-> pages

note right of chrome
  <b>Rule R2.</b> Persistent boxes inside #panel and #tabs never get a
  z-index: a hoisted box ignores clips from its ancestors and would
  paint over the toolbar when the panel scrolls.
  Ancestors of overlays get no opacity, transform or filter.
end note
note right of tips
  Hoisted layers are also hit-tested first,
  so the dropdown and the find box take
  clicks before the page under them.
end note
@enduml
